sec.p:
Once the optimal ICE torque is calculated, the ICE start-stop decision is optimized using DP in the next step. For a given equivalence factor, the equivalent fuel power consumption in hybrid mode $H_{hyb}$ and in electric mode $H_{elec}$ can be defined as follows:
\begin{align*} H_{hyb}& =\min \left ({{ P_{fuel}+s\cdot P_{elec} }}\right ) \tag {18}\\ H_{elec}& =s\cdot P_{elec} \tag {19}\end{align*}Accordingly, (13) is modified as follows:
\begin{align*} & J_{k}^{opt}\left ({{ \xi _{i}\left ({{ k }}\right ),{ss}_{ICE,j}\left ({{ k }}\right ) }}\right ) \\ & =\min _{u_{ss}\in U}\left [{{ \frac {1}{H_{u}}\mathrm {\cdot }H(k\mathrm {, }{ss}_{ICE,j}(k\mathrm {))\cdot \Delta }t+\dot {m}_{s}\left ({{ k,u_{ss}\left ({{ k }}\right ) }}\right )\cdot \Delta t }}\right . \\ & \quad \left .{{ +J_{k+1}^{opt}\left ({{ {ss}_{ICE,j}\left ({{ k+1 }}\right ) }}\right ) }}\right ] \tag {20}\\ & H\left ({{ k,{ss}_{ICE,j}\left ({{ k }}\right ) }}\right ) \\ & =\begin{cases} \displaystyle H_{hyb}, & \text {if}{ss}_{ICE,j}\left ({{ k }}\right )\mathrm {=1:ICE~ON} \\ \displaystyle H_{elec}, & \text {if}{ss}_{ICE,j}\left ({{ k }}\right )\mathrm {=0:ICE~OFF} \end{cases} \tag {21}\end{align*}
